      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The gametic model is often used when parental breeding values are of more concern than offspring values, as when one is attempting to estimate the breeding value of bulls from large arrays of descendants. In this model the additive genetic value of each offspring is expressed in terms of its parents' breeding values. In particular, letting $ a_{si} $ and $ a_{di} $ be the breeding values for individual i's sire and dam, we can express i's breeding value as",
      "source_page": 770,
      "printed_page": 750,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter26:p014:b3",
        "Genetics_chapter26:p014:b4"
      ],
