      "content_sha256": "f0d6817874ffa14a13124d0c446fe69d8cd5b5764586644cd645ed1548419eff"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Because they are random deviations around expectations, the segregation errors for all individuals are uncorrelated. Hence, the covariance matrix for the residual errors becomes",
      "source_page": 771,
      "printed_page": 751,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter26:p015:b2"
      ],
      "bbox": [
