        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "b0a5c23a7254b3cf919ecd902879475782859ff91f09fd91f4dacf0a2fe64221"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $\\mathbf{W}$ is a diagonal matrix with diagonal elements equal to $1 + (1 - \\overline{f}_i)/(2\\lambda)$, with $\\lambda = \\sigma_E^2 / \\sigma_A^2$ (as in the animal model). Note that $\\sigma_E^2 W_{ii}$ is the total within-family variance (the within-family segregation variance plus the within-family environmental variance).",
